{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1535184-classes-in-mage-yet-another-attempt","id":1535184,"title":"Classes in Mage- Yet Another Attempt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-05T14:04:41-07:00","id":1535184,"title":"Classes in Mage- Yet Another Attempt","content":"Something that I try to deal with every once and a while is finding a way to use Mage's system in order to represent a &quot;Class-like&quot; system- that is, using the base system in a hacked manner to represent different systems of spellcasting while drawing inspiration from D&amp;D and D&amp;D-derived systems to do so. The main motivation was always to find a flexible system in terms of magic using so I won't have to write whole classes for broad archetypical concepts, while still finding a way to ground them mechanically to a degree in a manner that gives them character and sense of uniqueness. After giving it a lot of thought and taking inspiration from Exalted: Essence, I think I found a way to represent the idea in a way which I like, and I thought to share it. Now, it is still very much a WIP and I am far from finishing this project, so feel free to give feedback about what you like and what you think can be improved.<br /> <br /> So, as it stands, each &quot;system of magic&quot; is represented through a <b>Call</b> (which is how a Class is called in this system). I currently started writing it from a fantasy setting's POV, which might explain certain things in the writeups and changes for certain terms, but it should be valid for a standard setting as well. As it stands, Calls replace to a degree both Paths and Orders by giving a philosophy, potential organization, yantra, Arcana access and Rote Skill Specialties, however as each Call also gives Attunements (which are the parallels for Advantages in ExEss), you could probably cut the overlapping elements and maintain the main parts without much of an issue. The way I envision Calls is them being much more specialized in terms of magic using, which give them more favored Arcana from one hand, more Inferior ones from the other, and plays around with Paradox to encourage a certain way in which magic is being cast. Also, each Call uses a different form of &quot;magical system&quot;, such as Divine, Arcane, Psychic, etc. As such, a Call Template is basically composed of the following-<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> description of the philosophy and methodology for magic by this Call<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening:</b> the common features in the Awakening for each of the Calls<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> description of how the Call is likely to view the search after enlightenment<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox:</b> description of how the class views Paradox as a phenomenon<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings:</b> basically Call Tool Yantra<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic:</b> the Ruling Arcana for the Call. There are tree of those, and no differentiation between Subtle and Gross<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic:</b> the Inferior Arcana for the Call. There are three of those in a similar manner to the Ruling ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills:</b> Rote Specialty Skills, choose 1 of three. One Skill is Mental, the other is Social and the third is Physical<br /> <br /> <b>Power Source:</b> the greater system from which this Call is derived.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunements:</b> 2 benefits which are unique to the Call. Using them does not invoke Paradox, and generally represent some useful tricks that the Call could use. Some sort of pseudo-Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing:</b> a special manner through which the Call might gain Arcane Beats<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse:</b> conditions for spellcasting that, when violated, increase the chance for Paradox<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, let's start with some examples- the Greater System (or <b>Paradigm</b>) of Divine Magic, as well as the first Call of that magic, the <b>Cleric</b>.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Divine- Magic Rules the World</b></i></u><br /> <br /> The power of the divine is, first and foremost, a bestowed one- it is the force of creation, which describes the celestial diagramas and draws power through the engines of the world. Due to its fundamental nature, divine magic holds a great power- yet also holds within it a great risk, for using the Divine Principles is a manner which disrupts their function draws the wrath of the world at best and a complete disaster at worst. As such, many religious organisations rise to properly supervise and hide divine secrets, though others work behind the scenes in order to patch out theological secrets and get their hands on this powerful magic, often forming strange kinds of cults around themselves in the process.<br /> \u200b<br /> <u><b>Cleric- Magic is a Dogma</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Bestowed upon by the gods, clerical magic revolves all around religion and dogma. Within this system, the cleric is used as a channel of the god\u2019s power, turning them into a vessel of a divine will. However, in order to gain access to divine magic, one has to resonate with the god which they worship. This requires both physical trappings, such as vestments, sacred colours and holy symbols, as well as behavioural rites, such as prayers, congregations and following a certain code of faith. However, the cleric doesn\u2019t need to actually believe in the god- only to resonate to a large enough degree that they embody the divine principles. This is because the gods are by themselves a product of religion, as the faithful are the ones who bestow upon them names and faces which, in turn, allow access to powers over the domains of reality- and as such, by embodying the religion, one does embody the god as well. However, many clerics do indeed believe in their gods and religion, for without a faith it becomes hard to maintain the necessary discipline which is required to resonate well with the god. On the other hand, clerics do depend on faith, for without believers who define the astral representations of the gods, the power of the cleric would flicker and die out. For that reason, if a cleric were to stray from their faith or the faith were to stray from them (by the believers changing their worldview), the cleric would find their power dwindling or even being completely denied. This is why the cleric needs a living religion in order to operate, and the size of the religion defining their power often decides the limits of their power. As each pantheon represents different values and rules over different domains, the exact capabilities of different clerics often vary to represent the nature of their divine patron and the values bestowed upon it.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening: </b>for the clerics, the Awakening is perceived as an instance of divine inspiration. As they are tied to the structural dogma which clothes them with power, all clerics are first members of their religion, and almost always are elevated to their status by their community. Their mystery play is initiated from within their congregation, and is often communal in nature, such as forcing the would be cleric to push their followers through a religious crisis, stopping their congregation from falling into infighting and vice, or following the wisdom of previous theologians in the effort to correctly manifest the will of their god. As such, when they finally Awaken, they do so as the representative of their community, cleansing the stains of the past and bridging the masses to the divine will.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> within the confines of clerical magic, enlightenment is associated with the gods. In order to properly invoke a divine power, a believer must delve into theological analysis, debating the nature of the gods and purpose behind their divine will. It means finding new representations of the divine, analysing old prophecies and texts written by the wise and conveying their sacred message to the masses. To truly understand the divine will is to become enlightened, which in turn would lead the masses towards enlightenment as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox:</b> Clerics are bestowed with great power, yet the gods do not share their power freely with the masses, else their name will be contaminated. According to the more religious practitioners of this magic, Paradox represents the ire of the gods for misusing their powers. Others, especially those who have become aware of the true nature of the gods, claim that paradox is merely a byproduct of using magic in a manner which contradicts the parameters of its source. As the god defines the values and principles which the magic is meant to fulfil (the so-called \u201cdivine will\u201d), violating those parameters would, in turn, allow magic to become corrupted, as there is no longer a force to correctly define it.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings:</b> prayers, sacred symbols, vestments, relics of saints, sacred texts.<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic:</b> Life, Mind, Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Forbidden Magic:</b> Matter, Space, Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills: </b>Religion, Persuasion, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Power Source:</b> Divine<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Word of God:</b> the cleric is a vessel of their god\u2019s power, and holds a special relation with their followers. The cleric gains free dots in Status (Religion) equal to their Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <b>Miracle Worker: </b>the cleric exists for their congregation, allowing them to ascend to the divine existence. They consider faithful of their religion to be sleepwalkers to the purpose of all works of magic used by them.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing:</b> whenever a cleric manages to support a significant character of their religion in a test of faith, they gain a Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse:</b> whenever the cleric casts a spell in a manner which violates the dogma of their religion (either in terms of it being used in an act which goes against their principles or that they act in a manner deemed as immoral) they gain +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T17:19:22-07:00","id":1535234,"title":"","content":"Putting up the next Call- the Oracle<br /> <br /> <u><b>Oracle- Magic is a Revelation</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> for many, the oracle is the voice of the gods upon earth. Chosen by the divine principles rather than earning their capabilities, the oracles are almost often heralded by omens, be them astronomical events, geological activities or even the patterns of beasts, plants and men. As such, all oracles are touched by magic before they were even born, though it may take them time to fully realise their own potential. As they commune directly with the divine principles, the magic of the oracles is vulgar in nature, embodying itself directly within the body, mind and soul of the oracle, leaving them forever marked and disfigured in a manner which forms a resonance with the divine principle. Those marks are often viewed as curses by young oracles, yet the more they develop their skills the more they learn to appreciate them as a connection to the divine. Integral to oracular magic is the idea of prophecy- when the oracle speaks, the world listens, for they bear within their voice their might and authority of the gods. Sometimes, even the oracle might not understand the power of their own prophecies, accidentally causing terrible damage as they learn to correctly tune the power of their speech. Knowing that their words bear power, many come to the oracles in search of blessings and curses, while others work to try and decipher their prophecies. As the oracle is a direct channel to the divine principles, their very presence tends to seep into the land, turning it to a divine site which draws the faithful towards them. As such, the oracle could never escape the burden of their revelation, making some despise the very principles which have arbitrarily chosen them due to the circumstances of their birth rather than their own choices.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening: </b>while all oracles are destined to Awaken, they are rarely prepared for the process itself. While some willworkers view magic as a delicate or nurturing force, for the oracles, magic is pain. The Awakening is a powerful, ecstatic and terrifying process in which the flesh and soul of the oracle are invaded by a will not their own which forces itself into them, leaving them scarred in the process. This, however, is only the climax of a long process- a mystery play initiated from the moment of their birth, as omens constantly manifest themselves around them in an attempt to draw their attention to the mysteries. Often, they are branded as mad, and are ostracised by their society as they attempt to understand the meaning of the mad world which surrounds them. While they may try and deny the call of the mysteries, it never goes away, and it is said that the longer it takes to follow it the more painful the revelation would be when it would finally be concluded.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis: </b>the world speaks to the oracles- the divine principles embody themselves into the world through the tapestry, whispering in their minds and revealing themselves through omens. In order to understand the hidden truth of the world, the oracle must follow the trail of mysteries, seek the hidden signs for the future and meditate on the will of the world itself. When they speak, it should be in tune with the world, so their very worlds would bear wisdom and allow the masses a glimpse of the divine, bridging the world of matter with that of divine inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox: </b>while the oracle speaks in the name of the gods, words can often become corrupted and twisted. Magic, after all, is already heavy with curses- one wrong word, and a would be blessing would doom a loved one and a would be curse would raise an enemy. The worst thing that one could do, in this instance, is lying- for the act of lies distorts the meaning of words, and as such violates the will of the gods. While many oracles learn trickery and use half truths or hide information in order to advance their desires, lies are almost always frowned upon, and those who act in a deceitful manner are punished by the gods for their hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: oracular tools, speaking in tongues, sacred texts, writing tools, musical instruments<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic:</b> Fate, Mind, Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Forces, Life, Matter<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills:</b> Enigmas, Expression, Survival<br /> <br /> <b>Power Source:</b> Divine<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessed Speech:</b> the voice of the oracles bear the might of the gods, and when they speak the masses listen. Spend one mana- for the rest of the scene, all of your social rolls gain the oracle\u2019s Gnosis as a modifier, up to 5.<br /> <br /> <b>House of the Gods:</b> the presence of the oracle overwrites reality\u2019s own nature, allowing the divine principle which they represent to freely embody itself. In order to create a demesne, the oracle needs one less soul stone than usual (which means that they can create a demesne of the lowest rank for free). This benefit can only be applied to one demesne at a time (so it can\u2019t be used for a new demesne as long as the previous one is still active)<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing:</b> choose a single Persistent Condition to represent the marking of the oracle\u2019s magic, be it physical, mental or spiritual. Whenever this Condition should grant you a beat, you gain an Arcane Beat instead. This condition can not be resolved, including through supernatural means.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse:</b> whenever the oracle casts a spell in a manner which either deceive others, promotes concealment of the truth in some manner, or while the oracle performs an act which embodies such values (such as hiding their identity or breaking a promise), gain +2 to the Paradox roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T17:59:18-07:00","id":1535235,"title":"","content":"Would a group of Oracles be able to stack the benefits of their abilities or only the first one to contribute to a Demesne would be counted ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T05:51:49-07:00","id":1535258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1535184-classes-in-mage-yet-another-attempt?p=1535235#post1535235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a group of Oracles be able to stack the benefits of their abilities or only the first one to contribute to a Demesne would be counted ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conceptually, the idea that each Oracle has their own oracular site, so I tend to say no in terms of the Attunement on its own. However, having a 1-5 rating Merit called &quot;Oracular Congregation&quot; or something like that that allows the advantage to be stacked sounds like a definite possibility (the &quot;design idea&quot; behind Attunements is that they give base abilities which should be further enhanced through Merits and such)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T13:41:39-07:00","id":1535671,"title":"","content":"Moving to the next Divine Call- adaptation of 4e Invokers<br /> <br /> <u><b>Invoker- Purity is Magical</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> the angelic choirs who regulate the celestial spheres are the direct manifestation of the divine will. Each angel is made to fulfil a certain mission- to heal or to harm, to bring love or misery. Every piece of existence has an angel governing it, while other angels exist to govern the smaller ones, creating a whole hierarchy of celestial order deriving all the way to the First Principles which brought creation into existence. As such, each person also has a guardian angel- a divine spirit meant to maintain their fate and guide their life in a manner which will be optimal for Heaven\u2019s service. While their presence is constant and vigil everlasting, most people are not aware of their own guardian angels, attributing instead the instances of their lives to their own choices or random chance. However, through sacred rites of purification, a person can not only become aware of their guardian angel but to unify with them- binding the divine spark to their own soul and as such gaining a hold over their own fate. This process makes the willworker into a celestial being, having the ability to invoke not only the power of their own fate but to call upon the might of the celestial hierarchy as a whole, for all angels are intertwined with one another through it. As such, invokers often maintain records of the countless angels which fill the skies, so they may correctly pronounce their divine names and manipulate the mechanisms of the world to their will. However, as divine beings, the invokers must maintain their purity and be wary of taint, as all angels are pure beings by themselves and despise taint. When faced with a world unworthy of their presence, weak angels would simply reject the call while stronger ones won\u2019t hesitate with cleansing the flawed reality, sometimes taking down the invoker along with it, hence why even the most powerful of invokers would be wary of calling upon the names of the rulers of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: for the invokers, the Awakening serves as their first invocation- a profound act of raw power where the willworker calls upon their own true name in order to force their guardian angel to reveal itself and bind with them. This invocation, however, does not come from nowhere- it requires a long process of effort and hard work as a person tries to understand their own fundamental nature and cleanse themselves from lower impurities. To connect with an angel, the would-be invoker must become like an angel- a pure vessel which does not fall victim to vice and hubris. Many invokers are seen as saints even before the invocation takes place, exemplars of virtues which resonate so deep that the difference between themselves and their higher being, the guardian angel, becomes smaller and smaller until through a declaration of their own will, the bridge is finally crossed and the two become one.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: with their eyes open to the celestial world, the invokers view the multitude of existence through the lenses of angelic properties- in order to affect an object, the invoker needs to understand their place within the divine hierarchy and correctly invoke the angels which are required to manipulate its fate. This takes the form of a long theological process, where the invoker learns how to position their own fate in relation to others, and as they bind more and more angels to their own name their influence on the world becomes more profound, allowing them to move the foundations of the world to benefit their will.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: serving as a bridge between the divine and the material, the invokers do not merely allow the celestial mechanism to affect the world of mortals, but also allow the material world to infect the divine purity. In order to avoid such instances, invokers regularly use purification rites and panacea ceremonies, yet even those who are the most careful about their own purity are still humans- and it is in the nature of humanity to fail. As such, when the angelic purity meets the taint of the material world, chaos erupts as the divine power rejects the faults of matter, and the standard of angels is very high, demanding the invoker to regularly keep their thoughts in check else instead of invoking the powers of Heaven they might bring forth the horrors of Hell.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: purification rituals, holy water and oil, fire, names of angels, summoning circles<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Fate, Forces, Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Death, Matter, Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Occult, Persuasion, Athletics<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Angelic Presence</b>: the invokers are tied to the divine hierarchies of Heaven, allowing them to command those whom they deem lesser. They have a Honorary Rank equal to their Gnosis (up to 5) in relation to angels, and are able to summon them as if they were Supernal Beings.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtuous Soul:</b> the invokers are exemplars of their virtues, allowing them to gain a greater sense of meaning from sacrifices in their name. They are able to fulfil their Virtue for Willpower twice per chapter, though the second time grants 1 Willpower instead of all Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: every time that you make a significant service to the powers of Heaven on the expense of your own benefit, gain an Arcane Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: when casting a spell in a manner which fulfils or resonates with your Vice or in a scene after which you failed an Act of Hubris roll, you gain +2 to the Paradox roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:32:46-07:00","id":1536067,"title":"","content":"Moving to the last Divine Call (the Templar) and some notes about how to adapt Calls to Modem and Fantasy settings.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Templar- Magic is a Shrine</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: divine magic is the infrastructure which feeds the world- and as such, the two are closely intertwined with one another. Even those without access to magical capacities are aware of it in the most instinctual manner- some places are simply viewed as hallowed, locations of pristine beauty which resonate deep within their souls in an almost instinctive manner. Those sacred places are where the veil grows thin, and the divine nature of reality becomes revealed to all, thriving freely with all of its magnificence. While many people are drawn to those places, those who disturb the sanctity of those locations are often devoured by them, for no such beauty is left without guardians to keep it from the unworthy. For the worthy, however, those fonts of divine power grant great power- crowning them as sacred guardians and shrine warriors which bear the power of the world itself in their hands. Each such templar warrior is chosen by the sacred location, binding their magic to the land itself. Though the templars draw power from their sacred shrines, they are not bound to those locations- though if they were to fall they would find their enlightenment flattering unless they would find a new place to bind themselves to. While some templars seek to understand the divine mechanism which allow such sacred places to rise so they could better protect them, others seek enlightenment in a more spiritual manner- their hallowed sanctuary has imbued them with power, after all, and within it are the visions of the perfected world which only they can see. The shrine represents the totality of the cosmos, after all- it is a world of itself, and the world as a whole, and the soul of the templar themselves, as they are imbued with the divine power and embody themselves in the shrine. To rule upon the shrine is to become the ruler of the world, and to let it fall would mean to lose oneself into an eternal darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: the places which the templars come to view as shrines existed long before the templar was ever born and, hopefully, would remain long after their death. As those places are fonts of divine magic by themselves, many mysteries are embodied within them, and each serves as its own mystery play for those who dare to enter their borders. More than other Awakenings, the templar Awakening is considered deadly, for a few wrong steps would lead the would-be spellcaster to be devoured by the magic they sought to tame as they venture to worlds beyond the physical reality. Those who triumph, however, do so by binding their soul to the heart of the sacred place, and as the two become one, the Awakening is achieved.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: each of the templars shares a metaphysical connection to the place in which they Awakened, making the two into one. As such, the soul of the templar exists within the location, and by understanding the divine symbols which are embodied within it new enlightenment can be achieved. This leads many templars to carefully tend and cultivate their hallowed shrines, further embodying their own humanity and personality within the primordial space as they search after their own place in the world and attempt to understand themselves. According to their own philosophy, the whole world is contained within the shrine, and as such the true knowledge of the world can only be achieved by understanding their shrine, which means, first and foremost, understanding themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: the difference between a garden and the wilderness is defined by one trait- love. The garden is carefully cultivated and tended for, the objects within it are carefully arranged and the atmosphere is decided by the gardener. The wilderness is raw and untamed, harsh and violent. The garden serves as a small gateway to the wilderness, a place meant to serve the will of the gardener with all of their heart, yet the wilderness is constantly lurking beneath the surface, waiting to emerge with all of its glory once the gardener would let their guard down. The shrine is the garden of magic, and the templar is the gardener, who maintains a small piece of divine magic stabilised within the empyreal chaos of divine magic. Stop tending the garden, and the divine wilderness would quickly take over the heart and soul of the templar.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: ritual weapons, gardening tools, altars, warding symbols, soil from a sacred ground.<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Life, Prime, Space<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Death, Fate, Time<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Crafts, Expression, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Soul of the World</b>: through the process of their Awakening, all templars are connected to a Hallow which bestows power upon them. Their Hallow is of a rating equal to their Gnosis and it grows in power accordingly, and they can draw mana from it through Oblation even when not in its boundaries. In case their Hallow is somehow lost, they can anchor themselves to a new one if its rating is equal or lesser than their Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <b>Twilight Reach</b>: as sacred warriors bestowed with divine power, templars can reach beyond the boundaries of their flesh. Spend one mana and choose a certain frequency of the Twilight- until the end of the scene, you can interact with objects of that frequency as if they were materialised.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: each time the templar makes a significant sacrifice or effort in order to protect or maintain their Hallow, they gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: when casting spells outside the domain of their Hallow and without having mana gained from it in their Mana pool, gain +2 to Paradox rolls. <b>Settings</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Modern Setting</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Clerics</b>: rising across all systems of faith, the clerics are generally derived from the Obrimos and Mastigos Paths, discovering their Awakening through a mystery play centred around the imagery of demons and angels. Being so close to their local communities, many clerics are Nameless, finding a safe haven within the Free Council as they lead their communities as a whole towards Ascension. However, just as many seem to focus more around dogma and control as magical symbols, joining the Seers of the Throne which they claim to serve as the \u201ctrue gods\u2019 through myriad astral descriptions of those dark entities, with the Paternoster Ministry hosting the vast majority of those Awakened. Outside of those tyrannical faiths, clerics often use astral manifestations of their own faith, with the most devoted turning their attention towards the mysterious Aeons, which they claim to be the true gods of humanity, forever lurking at the edge of the Fallen as they wait for the Supernal to finally bridge the Abyss once more.<br /> <br /> <b>Oracles</b>: most common among the Obrimos and Acanthus Paths, the oracles are highly revered across the different Orders of the world. For the Seers, they are the mouths of the Exarchs, pronouncing dread prophecies in the name of the Prophet. Among the Diamond, they are the voice of the Watchtowers, speaking Supernal truths into existence while overriding the Lie. Many are also found in the centre of cults dedicated to the Old Gods, with the Bound drawing those Awakened to serve as their messengers and heralds beyond the boundaries of their prison. Strangely, quite a few oracles end up in service to the Ascending Ones, acting as their sacred prophets who teach them the secrets of alchemy through divine revelation while their dread prophecies are recorded to be used in their war against the darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Invokers</b>: holding a strange affinity to the occult mechanism known as the God Machine, many invokers are found away from the Awakened society, instead acting as agents of the dread god or serve within the cults which work to usurp it. The Deva Corporation and Raziel Ltd by their own hold a few Obrimos invokers in their service, employing their skills in order to take over infrastructures and bind angels to their will. Still, there are a significant number of Invoker within the Orders as well- among the Seers, most join Paternoster and serve the Father of Angels, while those who join the Diamond find acceptance among either the Mysterium, where their knowledge in angelology is highly renowned, or among the Silver Ladder, who use this symbolism in order to invoke the divine system of ruling Heaven and Earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Templars</b>: with each templar generally residing near a Hallow, the templars are generally a scattered folk, preferring to work as Nameless rather than joining any of the Orders. Their strong affinity to those sacred places means that the vast majority of templars are derived from the Obrimos Path, though a few are Thyrsus who find resonance within loci and other spiritual places. While their localised nature is what keeps most of them away from Awakened politics, another reason why they mostly avoid joining the Orders comes from how many mages seek to drain Hallows for mana, viewing it as resources while acting with little to no respect. As such, templars often clash against those who try to violate their temples, which leads to a strange trend where numerous templars end up becoming Banishers, working to cleanse the world from those who do not honour it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Fantasy Setting</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Clerics</b>: holding monopoly over religion and faith, the Pantheistic Church is a bureaucratic mechanism containing countless small cults, religious orders and theological academies. In order for a faith to be publicly practised, it must be recognised by the Church, which establishes its holidays, festivals and sacred sites under its protection- and roots out any faith which acts \u201cout of line\u201d and \u201cwithout proper permission\u201d. Still, the Church allows a relatively wide freedom of faith for religions who take part within it, mostly making sure that clerics of faith do not abuse their power and authority and that there are no illegal acts which defy the kingdom (and the Church\u2019s) authority- all for the protection of the public, of course. While numerous small gods take part in the system, the Eleven Great Gods (often known as the Aeons) are the ones who serve as the pillars of the Church, who are worshipped by hundreds of thousands of souls as they pray for their blessings and favours.<br /> <br /> <b>Oracles</b>: rising unexpectedly all across the kingdom, the oracles are highly revered and often feared by the simple people. Plagued with madness and riddled with curses, their Awakening is seen as an ominous sign, both a blessing and a curse for their community. Due to their direct connection to the gods, the Pantheistic Church constantly seeks to regulate the oracles, building a whole mechanism known as the Omen Watcher Orders which seeks out the signs for new oracles and acts quickly to track down and take those willworkers into \u201ctraining\u201d as soon as they Awaken. This helps make sure that the prophecies of the oracles will be maintained under strict watch while giving the Church the needed monopoly over prophecy, making sure that the gods will not disrupt the religions which maintain them. Still, many communities do value the existence of a divine channel to the divine, and work to hide their oracles from the Orders, maintain small illegal cults far from the watching eye of the Church.<br /> <br /> <b>Invokers</b>: found deep within the halls of the Church\u2019s sacred libraries, the Order of the Divine Providence is barely known to the wide public. Those few outsiders to the Church who do know about it simply think of it as an order of theologians who invest their time researching divine knowledge. Within the Church, however, the invokers of the Order are both honoured and feared. Tasked with maintaining the sacred mechanisms who maintain the world, very few people are allowed to join the Order and study their sacred rites, for misuse of their secrets might unleash terrible cataclysms upon the world. Still, there are rumours of copies of the sacred rites used by the Order circling outside of its constant vigil, spread by rogue invokers or thieves who managed to lay their hands on the sacred texts. While the Church officially denies the existence of such grimoires, even a whisper about the existence of such a grimoire outside of the Order\u2019s control or an invoker who acts independently is enough to mobilise the Church\u2019s forces in rooting out the threat.<br /> <br /> <b>Templars</b>: as part of the Church\u2019s duty of maintaining shrines and temples all across the kingdom, the Warrior Orders of the Sacred Throne serve as the most valued tool in this mission. As a whole, the Orders are tasked with finding sites touched by the divine, building shrines around them and maintaining their integrity against the ravages of time and fighting against threats. Within the kingdom proper, the Warrior Orders are more of a symbol of status than an actual necessity, dealing mostly with acts of mischief from the public and potential vandalism from heretics. At the outskirts of the kingdom, however, they are the kingdom\u2019s main tool at advancing into the wilderness, taking over new sacred sites, expanding the kingdom\u2019s faith to locals and protecting shrines built in untamed lands beyond the major cities. There, the templars have to fight on a daily basis against not only raiding bandits, hungry monsters and ravaging marauders, but also against the templars chosen by those sites long before the Church tried to claim them as its own, who will not simply allow their sacred places be taken by the insatiable, power hungry kingdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T15:08:10-07:00","id":1536220,"title":"","content":"So moving to the next &quot;magic type&quot;, we have the Sacrilegious Magic- which is a concept for &quot;dark divine magic&quot;, yet not necessary a evil one. Alongside it, we have the first Sacrilegious Call- the Envoys, who are a take on the templar class from Dark Sun.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sacrilegious- Magic is Deviance (Rust)</u></b><br /> <br /> Across many different nations, sacrilegious magic is considered to be illegal- and for a good reason. This system acts in a parasitic manner, working as if it was a leech draining the flow of creative power from the celestial infrastructure which produces divine magic. If divine magic describes the laws which govern the process of endless creation, sacrilegious magic acts against those laws, violating the systems by creating their own systems which override the rules of the divine hierarchy to drain divine magic. As such, the use of this magic is always metaphysically abhorrent, as the divine light which should have benefited the natural order of the world is stolen for the selfishness of mortal will. Still, due to this magic being unconstrained by the laws of Heaven, it is considered much flexible to use, allowing mortals to decide the laws instead of relying on the arbitrary will of the Powers that Be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Envoy- Service is Magical</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: the difference between a mortal and a god is not a matter of origin or nature- it is a matter of power. To be a god is to have the power to shape the world- to elevate mortals to greatness or to decree them to death, to bless the land with wealth or to deny it. The one to rule the land is the one who is like god- and if that\u2019s so, who is a better candidate to be a god than the ruler of the land? Kings and queens, presidents and chancellors- their laws are the ones who decree the fate of the world, whole mechanisms operating around them to make sure that their will is fulfilled. This is the Divine Rights of Kings- a divine mandate forming around them, turning them into vessels of divine power. However, while the kings hold the power, they can only extract their influence through the mechanisms built around them. As such, by becoming an envoy to the king\u2019s power, one becomes part of the infrastructure which surrounds them- and draws divine power in exchange for their service. This creates a strange balance of power- for while the system requires the king in order to produce divine magic by creating a symbolic representation of the divine hierarchy, the will of the king does not actually matter within the system. They are gods trapped in their own shell, with their will being processed and modified into laws and regulations through the bureaucracy that surrounds them, allowing envoys to rise without the king\u2019s will or even awareness, who might even abuse the system and go against its laws to fulfil their own desires.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: to become an envoy one first must become a part of the organisation- only those who are part of the bureaucratic system are able to extract its power, yet not many are aware of the true potential hidden within it. As such, the mystery play of those who would become envoys relies on understanding the true secrets of their organisation- hidden conspiracies, coccults symbolism embedded into the system of rule, strange dealings with stranger beings and obscure laws are all ways through which the mysteries reveal themselves to the envoy, and eventually are concluded by contractual obligation to the dark forces which operate those conspiracies behind the scenes in heaven and earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: to the envoy, occult knowledge is embedded into the fabric of legalistic procedures which maintain the organisation running. To define one's place within the bureaucracy and how the laws affect them is to free them from its bindings, while utilising the same mechanisms against their enemies would allow them to bind them to their will. As such, many envoys spend hours learning the different legal mechanisms of the state and how they interact with each other, as well as how different legal systems interact with one another to create a complicated web of divine power, ready to reap.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: in the end, the system which envoys operate is, by nature, a flawed system- it is a false infrastructure created as a mockery to Heaven, producing divine magic artificially and without the consent of the king who stands at its middle. As such, it is a little wonder that sometimes, the system fails. While the envoy may be able to regulate it to a degree by maintaining the integrity of the laws under which they operate and make sure that they don\u2019t violate the regulations which keep the state running, this is merely a patchwork on the true issue which can not and will not be fixed- that while mortal may claim themselves to be as gods, this would never be true, and claiming otherwise is merely an act of hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: contracts describing the involved parties, legal texts, symbols of the sovereign powers, regalia, national symbols<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Fate, Matter, Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Death, Prime, Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Politics, Persuasion, Stealth<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Mandate of Heaven</b>: the envoy is part of the bureaucratic systems which create the mockery of heaven, giving them instinctual power over it. They treat their Gnosis score as an effective Status (Organization) score in relation to the mechanism that they represent, such as a ministry of the government, a certain company of choice or similar organisation.<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Utility</b>: the envoys recognize the inherent value that abstract rule has, and are able to drain the mechanisms which operate the state for their utility. By spending time through bureaucratic work related to their role within the state, they can make an Oblation roll as if it was a Hallow with a rating equal to its effective Standing (see Deviant), up to 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing:</b> whenever you successfully complete a significant service to the organisation which you serve, gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: whenever you cast spells which violate the laws and regulations which the organisation employs, or if you have fallen off the organisation\u2019s grace, you gain +2 to the Paradox roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T18:03:53-07:00","id":1536223,"title":"","content":"Would there be any chance you could do a Merchant Call ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T10:02:45-07:00","id":1536262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1535184-classes-in-mage-yet-another-attempt?p=1536223#post1536223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there be any chance you could do a Merchant Call ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while I didn't plan to, and doing so did require me to make a new Power Source (currently called &quot;Hedge Magic&quot;, referring to the use of magic in a manner which is indirect and relying on mundane materials), here is a version of a Merchant Call- the Broker:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Broker- Magic Demands a Price</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: the world is filled with riches- shiny rocks buried beneath the soil, precious metals waiting to be harvested, luxurious food hiding in plain sight. Everything has a value, it just needs to be evaluated according to those who want it compared to those who have it. As such, objects only have a value as long as they are needed- once the need meets the demand, the value is gone, yet the greater the distance between the two the more profit one would achieve by coordinating this connection. This is the job of the willworker- for if everything has a value, then by coordinating the desires of the world to the items who would satisfy it one could ignite the primordial spark and draw the profit out of the abstract value. Through profit, one gains the greatest benefit of all- agency, the capacity to change the world to your desires and gain freedom from the bindings of the world. After all, magic is by itself a pure value, and when used to pay to the gods one could avoid their wrath, maintaining balance and gaining access to their domains. Break the scales, however, and the world would lash upon you, demanding the price which was stolen from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: for the brokers, the Awakening always has a cost- it is something that was earned, not through devotion or faith, but through hard, cold money. Their mystery play comes into action as part of a financial risk- people losing their house, getting fired from their job, descending into piles of debt. The world keeps on biting on them, taking more and more and leaving little behind. The world owes them- yet it refuses to pay the price. Screaming against the unfairness of the world, the brokers start working towards getting their proper compensation. They delve deep into the mysteries, negotiating with the Powers that Be to balance the scales. Through cleverness and trickery, and put the gods in debt to them- and with no other way to absolve themselves from it, the Awakening is granted, making the broker free of their own debts as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: knowledge, like everything else in the world, has its value. Everyone needs something- people need food, plants need the sun, fire needs wood and entropy needs to rise. By Understanding the relation between the different needs of different entities, the broker can understand both what is the value of the desired object and how much they can gain by trading it. The ability to produce good deals depends on this ability to appraise an object\u2019s value, which requires of the broker to understand not only the desires of people (not to mention the powers which govern the world), but also the inherent value that every object might has, and what is the optimal way to correlate the supply and the demand in a manner which would maximise profit. In the end, ascension is merely one more deal- the ultimate deal, perhaps, which would grant godhood to the broker, but a deal nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: greed is the bane of all brokers. Focused on maximising their profits, they start to lose sight of making sure that the needs are fulfilled and more about how much they can gain. However, what they forget is that they are not playing a fair fight- the social contract which allows them to trade with the world is only as valid as long as their customers are willing to accept it. While trading with mortals has little consequences, when the gods are exploited they are quick to demand vengeance- after all, the king could, at any moment, change the value of the currency, nationalise businesses, employ regulations and tariffs or just take over the wealth that the brokers have gathered. It is only by their good graces that the economy is maintained, and if they feel violated then the gods would be quick to punish the rogue broker with all of their wrath.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: currency, jewellery and luxurious clothes, rare spices, contracts signed by the broker, handshakes<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Fate, Matter, Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Forces, Life, Time<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Politics, Persuasion, Ride<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>A Vulture\u2019s Eye</b>: brokers are well versed in reading their customers, and are able to easily find cracks in their resolve. When performing Social Manoeuvres related to making a bargain of some sort (that is, gaining something in exchange for something of a proper value) and they do not try to cheat or mislead the other party, they add a bonus equal to their Gnosis to the rolls, and they can always attempt making Social Manoeuvers (meaning, the lowest their Impression can go effectively is Average)<br /> <br /> <b>Riches of the World</b>: brokers have access to the wellspring of potential through their vast wealth, and can easily find the proper trade that would grant them what their heart desires. They can use their Resources rating as a yantra, adding a bonus equal to their Resources score. Doing so, however, reduces their effective Resources by one (minimum of zero), and it takes one session in order to restore the rating by one dot.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: whenever you successfully complete a deal which satisfies both parties for either a significant product for themselves or in service for a significant character, they gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: whenever you cast a spell around a target which you cheated, lied to or deceived without paying a proper compensation, or you are in a scene when you have recently did such an act, you gain +2 to the Paradox roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T16:33:46-07:00","id":1536320,"title":"","content":"Moving to the next Sacrilegious Call, we have the Heretic- a iteration of the Ur Priest Prestige Class:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Heretic- Magic Must Be Taken</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: the divine forces which operate the world are aloof and uncaring. Within the celestial scheme, mortals simply don\u2019t matter- they are a flow of light which keeps flowing from the source of souls and into the pits of Hell. Reaching enlightenment is practically impossible, dooming the vast majority of humans into a life of suffering and tyranny, unable at grasping their own fate. The system is flawed- yet that Powers That Be can\u2019t care less about it. The magic which they use to maintain the flow of creation is jealousy kept yet arbitrarily divided, allowing evil to prosper while the just are left in misery. The system is simply not fair- and as such, it must be challenged. It must be broken. By committing transgressions against the laws of heaven, the system which maintains the world slowly unravels- and where cracks are formed, the divine light starts leaking, allowing those who are ready to capture the power of creation and use it for their own needs. While many would claim that such acts of transgression are immoral, when the system itself is unjust breaking it apart is the only just thing. Mortals should reach and claim their own fate, free from divine tyranny and false perceptions of morality. By forcing their own will upon the world, true freedom could be achieved, releasing those who dare to challenge the system as the kings of this world. The system, obviously, would try to get rid of those individuals, yet one can not expect a tyrant to sit idly while they lose their force. Step by step, the system will break down, giving humans the freedom they deserve so much, becoming gods of their own worlds.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: the heretical Awakening is always found in antithesis to another, greater force. A person is chased down by a system- something which is larger and greater than them and which seeks to bring them down. Most people would comply with the great power, recognizing that they are powerless to stand against it. The would-be heretic, however, is different- their mystery play is initiated as an act of rebellion against the unfair, uncompromising force, regardless of the chances. As they struggle, symbols of challenge and retribution start gathering, leading them in the footsteps of the great revolutionaries of history. The rebellion, however, will fail- as all rebelion do. There, broken and bleeding, when all fails, the soul must take the challenge and spit in the face of god- and by doing so, they would finally become true heretics, finding them freedom they so dearly desire.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: the ideal that all heretics desire towards is, in essence, freedom- they wish to break their own chains from the bindings of the world, becoming free souls who create heavens of their own. As such, heretics explore their own vices, especially those who are associated with the religious paradigms within which they grew. By violating taboos, they test their own strength of will against that of society, going against the norms by freeing themselves from mental bindings imprinted upon them while they were still asleep. Each such act of transgression allows the heretic to learn something about themselves, explain whether they avoid an act due to their own desires or those forced upon them, and as such, advance their path towards true, unlimited freedom.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: you can\u2019t steal from the gods and not expect consequences. The powers of Heaven are jealous beings, who fear the idea of man becoming like gods by eating both the fruits of knowledge and life. To protect themselves from the greedy mortals, they send against them the Hounds of Heaven- they make magic revolut and break, send their angels to punish the ungrateful souls and even turn the world itself against the spellcaster as punishment for their acts of retribution. It might be easier to simply comply with those laws, yet by doing so the gods will trap you. Instead, the heretic must assert dominance, denying the ability of Heaven to rule their lives. By denying the law, the heretic is free- by accepting them- the gods would yank the chain.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: the seven deadly sins, desecrated religious symbols, heretical texts, acts which violate social taboos, bodily mutilations<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Mind, Prime, Space<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Death, Fate, Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Investigation, Subterfuge, Larceny<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Serpent\u2019s Tongue</b>: heretics are tempters by nature, and easily notice the faults in human nature. When trying to either analyse a person\u2019s Vice or equivalent or when using it in social rolls, they gain a bonus to the roll equal to their Gnosis, up to +5.<br /> <br /> <b>Stealing Heaven\u2019s Light</b>: heretics are well versed in breaking the system of Heaven, allowing them to leech the divine light for their own purposes. While performing an act which is considered a social or religious taboo in a public manner, they can roll to Oblation as if they were draining mana from a Hallow.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: whenever you put yourself or your goals in a significant risk or burden by going against a system of rule, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: whenever you cast magic in a manner which knowingly serves the interests of a greater agenda, be it a religious or a political one, on the expense of your own interests, you gain +2 to the Paradox roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T16:06:19-07:00","id":1536389,"title":"","content":"Next Call we have a rework of the Archivist class from 3e, with a new name- the Theurge<br /> <br /> <u><b>Theurge- Magic Must be Archived</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: the divine systems which operate the world are impossible to be fully understood- the truth is always outside of reach, with any attempt to describe it is doomed to fail. However, that also means that all ways to describe the truth are all equivalently true- and as such, the secrets for the divine could be found within every piece of religious text, every pronounced prophecy and every strange dream about the worlds beyond. As such, the true nature of magic can be extrapolated from the numerous works that humanity has produced in an attempt to understand it, be it religious, scientific or artistic. Only through a holistic attitude, one which encompasses the multitude of human knowledge, a path to the truth can be opened, and the mortal soul could be exposed to the divine. Yet, the fact still stands that the truth can not be achieved- and even by collecting the scattered secrets of humanity and constructing them into a cohesive form this would produce a mere model, not the truth itself- a path which is both personal and flawed, yet reaches out to achieve greatness. This symbol of the truth provides a channel to the divine system, a diagram of its celestial magnificent which holds within it the path for godhood, and by finding their own path to the divine, theurges are able to become gods of their own world, reaching out to the heavens and be like god.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: for the theurge, the Awakening always takes the form of an obsession- a certain detail stands out of place, a small verse becomes alluring, or a sudden moment of divine realisation strikes after reading the same prayer for countless times. This small detail slowly starts to become a pattern, as more and more of those instances start showing up across numerous texts and works written by the wisest of the past. Slowly and surely, the quest for knowledge becomes all consuming, as the desire to understand the pattern goes out of control and the search for a way to tie them all together becomes unbearing. Many can not withstand the overtaxing price of the long hours of research, their souls shatter and as they fall into the depths of despair. Those who do triumph do so by accepting that the true meaning of their path would forever avoid them, and that only by witnessing the divine magnificence they could know it, even if their description would forever be flawed.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: among all willworkers, the theurges truly believes in the value of knowledge on itself- there is no such thing as useless information, for every work which humanity has produced might hold within it a secret representation of the divine. To gain a deeper understanding of reality, the spellcaster must understand how previous generations have seen it, and then tie it to their own model of the truth. While their path to the divine is their own unique creation, born in the fire of their Awakening, this model must evolve with time, growing and changing as new secrets about the truth are revealed to the miracle worker. Let the path remain stagnant for too long, and it is only a matter of time before the rot would start spreading.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: there is no greater danger to the wonder maker than believing that they have reached a complete understanding of the world. By assuming that their quest for truth has been achieved, the theurge would falsely assume that there is no more knowledge to collect, and that they hold in their hands the ability to shape the world. This, however, is merely a hubris- no theurge has ever found a complete understanding of the divine, and they never will. By pronouncing their own false imitation of the truth as the truth itself, the theurge commits a sin against the world by forming a divine paradox- the false is claimed to be true, and as such the truth must be false. Ignore the call of heaven and its challenges to your worldview, and all you could expect is your path to fall down, proving that the model has reached its limits.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: religious texts, cosmological diagrams, religious symbols, theological arguments, models of the universe<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Fate, Mind, Space<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Death, Forces, Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Investigation, Expression, Survival<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Eye to the Strange</b>: theurges know that they must always keep one eye open to the mysteries of the world, for the truth always waits to be found. When attempting to solve a Mystery, the number of successes required as determined by its Opacity is reduced by the theurgist\u2019s Gnosis (up to five), to a minimum of one per roll. The number of successes is reduced from the highest Opacity rating first, and any excess reduction is moved to the next lower rank.<br /> <br /> <b>Diagram of Heavens</b>: every theurge builds their own path towards enlightenment, using the wisdom of others to feed their own. When learning a Rote spell, the theurge can decide to learn it as a Praxis instead. If they learn it as a Praxis through both means, it is considered to have the benefits of a Rote and a Praxis simultaneously.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: whenever you discover information which forces them to perform a significant reconsideration of their current philosophy or worldview, gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: whenever you refuse are faced with the possibility you were wrong about a subject of your proficiency, you gain the Cognitive Dissonance Condition. This Condition grants a +2 to all Paradox rolls, and is solved by finding a way to connect the new fact to the worldview you held.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T10:26:48-07:00","id":1536445,"title":"","content":"And for the last Sacrilegious Call- the Penitent<br /> <br /> <b><u>Penitent- Magic is a Punishment</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: the Original Sin was the act of biting the Fruit of Knowledge against God\u2019s Will- all was for humanity to claim and to rule, yet falling to temptations they wished to become like God, and as punishment, they fell from grace. Every act of magic is a replication of this sin- for the powers of the divine are beyond mortal\u2019s grasp, and every attempt at claiming them is doomed to not only fail, but bring the world down with it. And yet, the Fruit of Knowledge is humanity\u2019s desire- it was made in the image of the gods, and was born out of the primordial earth and the divine wind. As such, the act of demanding magic is part of human nature, though punishment must accompany it to satisfy the forces of Heaven. As no act of magic goes unpunished, one can not avoid its wrath- however, they can choose the punishment. By offering a sacrifice before Heaven, one would satisfy the Powers That Be- and with the spellcaster being the sacrifice, they are able to choose their own punishment and avoid the wrath of the Heavenly Host. This allows the enlightened soul to replicate the act of the Original Sin and embody it within themselves- becoming a living vessel for humanity\u2019s sins and sacrificing themselves as a punishment so they could grasp at the forbidden knowledge of Heaven. While this replication allows one to go through the Gates of Paradise and enjoy the Fruits of Life and Knowledge, one should still be wary to make sure that Heaven is satisfied with the proposed punishment- else, the wrath of Heaven would grow sevenfold, throwing the would be god into the pits of Heaven in their hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b>: for the Penitent, the Awakening is not a reward- it is a punishment. Their very existence is a monument for humanity\u2019s hubris, a daring attempt to claim divine magnificence only to fall into the depths of pain. Each future Penitent starts with a fall of grace- before their Awakening, they were the best and finest of humanity, standing at the top echelons of society. In their hands, they held the power to decree the fate of thousands of souls, or they lavished on the wealth that they or their ancestors gathered, or possibly just been the greatest of their area of expertise, well renowned among their community. Then, the fall begins- everything falls apart, and there is little to no control over it. Every attempt they make to stop the collapse fails, or is even turned against them, as if a vengeful god has decreed their failure. Most are crushed by the events, unable to withstand the pressure. Those who seek meaning for their failure, however, start noticing the omens which brought their fall- they follow their own mystery play, trying to understand why did they deserve this punishment, until eventually, they come across the judge who decreed their punishment, and by accepting the verdict, they can become a vessel to humanity\u2019s sin- and with it, the gift of magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b>: the gods are not kind beings- on the contrary, they are petty, vengeful and envious beings, constantly seeking to maintain their throne and tame humanity through cruel punishments and laws of suffering. However, as they are indeed petty and envious beings, they can be easily satisfied through self inflicted punishment to what they conceive as \u201csin\u201d- those who punish can never usurp their thrones, after all. As such, the penitents work to understand the cruel laws of the gods and which punishments would satisfy them- within their pain, they find enlightenment, and within their sins, they find salvation. Find yourself a worthy punishment, and the gods won\u2019t bother at inflicting one on you. Take upon yourself the sins of the world, and the only way to reward you will be ascension.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b>: the very act of using magic is an immoral one- a primordial sin judged by the gods. As such, it is little wonder that using it would bring punishment. The gods often rage against those acts of hubris, and while learning the criteria which would keep them satisfied helps to keep them in bay, eventually they will feel the urge to put them those who, in their opinion, grew beyond their limits and need to \u201cbe brought down a notch\u201d. As such, every act of magic bears the risk of getting punished by Heaven, and while they can be satisfied to a degree eventually, they will bring down their own verdict, causing your magic to get out of control.<br /> <br /> <b>Trappings</b>: panacea rituals, scourges, bodily mutilations, fasting, chains and locks<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Magic</b>: Death, Life, Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Banned Magic</b>: Fate, Spirit, Prime<br /> <br /> <b>Speciality Skills</b>: Medicine, Empathy, Survival<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunements</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Sin Eater</b>: penitents are ceremonial scapegoats, sacrifices for humanity\u2019s collective sins- and as such, are able to absorb them. When a character fulfils their Vice or equivalent near them, they can spend one mana in order to gain an amount of Willpower equal to their Gnosis, while the original character does not gain any benefit. This is still considered a use to fill their Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Willing Sacrifice</b>: penitents are used to be used as a sacrifice by the world, and as such know the depths of pain greater than any mortal mind could imagine. They do not suffer from wound penalties.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnostic Blessing</b>: whenever you willingly subject yourself to a significant amount of suffering, pain or self sacrifice, you gain an Arcane Beat. In case the act would fulfil your Virtue, you need to choose between gaining Willpower and the Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradoxical Curse</b>: whenever you cast magic without causing yourself a significant act of pain or suffering, be it physical, mental or emotional, you gain +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <u><b>In the Setting</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Modern Setting</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Envoys</b>: integrated deep into the power structures of both the mortal and Awakened worlds, most of the Envoys are derived from the Mastigos and Acanthus Paths. Quite a few are naturally drawn to the Seers of the Throne, mostly taking interest in the Ministries of the Prophet and the Unity, though the Chancellor has a growing membership of those spellcasters. In the Diamond, however, the envoys are almost exclusively a part of the Silver Ladder, using their symbols of rule to manifest their divine right upon the Awakened society. A few, however, choose independent paths, getting intertwined with mortal conspiracies such as Task Force: VALKYRIE, the R.A.M or Section 9, working behind the scenes to maintain the power of their nations.<br /> <br /> <b>Heretics</b>: almost exclusively Mastigos (though a few Obrimos do adopt the Call as well), the vast majority of the heretics walk the Left Handed Path. Their members worship the Lower Depths, take part in the Ziggurat of the Scelesti or just walk the dark way to the Enrapture, with some even become intertwined with stranger mysteries, such as the God Machine and the Unchained cults which escape it, seeing them as kindred souls. The Seers at large mostly despise heretics, with a few following the mysterious Gate while hiding their true nature. In the Diamond, they could mostly be found within the Mysterium, though some find interest in the self-destructive rites of the Guardians of the Veil. The Nameless do contain the most sane of heretics, specifically among those who fall paths of ecstasy in the Free Council.<br /> <br /> <b>Theurges</b>: derived from the Masrtigos and Acanthus Paths, the vast majority of theurges are divided between the Free Council and the Mysterium. In the Free Council, the theurges mostly adopt all kinds of strange Nameless paradigms, using the techne which defines the Order as part of their personal paths towards enlightenment and often freely argue with each other in an attempt to share ideas about the true nature of reality. In the Mysterium, on the other hand, the theurges are treated as a living proof that magic is, indeed, alive- by collecting the scattered secrets of the Supernal within their archives and working together to produce different paradigms about the nature of the Supernal World, they allow magic to grow and prosper, allowing it to slowly create the path of knowledge which would bridge the Supernal to the Fallen and would finally eliminate the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <b>Penitents</b>: obsessed with sin and self punishment, most penitents find themselves at home among the Guardians of the Veil. Their rituals which degrade humanity and bear sin by mutilating both mind and flesh as a form of enlightenment resonate well with the value of those strange Awakened, allowing them to practise their awful rites far from watching eyes while presenting a composed face to the outside world. As such, the Mastigos and Moros who adopt this Call are among the most devoted of the Guardians, making them among the most dangerous ones as well. Outside the Diamond, however, there are many Penitents who just follow their own paths among the Nameless, though many of those end up turning to the Left Handed Paths, becoming Scelesti or accidentally break their souls to become Enraptured. There are also a few of their members among the Seers, members of Exarchial cults who seek to satisfy the Kings of the Lie in a manner which would allow them access to magic, and most of their members join the ministries of the Eye and the Ruin.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Fantasy Setting</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Envoys</b>: the Wings of the Throne is the name granted to the diplomatic wing of the kingdom, serving the king and the court of nobles through their political manoeuvres. Most of the envoys who serve in the wings are either lesser nobles or elevated commoners, never people from the upper echelons of society yet always close to them. As part of the kingdom\u2019s feudal system, each member of the Wings personally serves one of the nobles, and more often than not their interests work against those of others in the Wings. Still, envoys are not bound forever to their nobles, as the king is the one who distributes them, and can either elevate or demote them according to their will. The most renowned ones serve the king and the royal family directly, while those of the lowest rank are sent to local field nobles, who are barely better than commoners themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Heretics</b>: the Left Handed Coven is among the most dreaded of cults which the kingdom has to deal with- while some of those illegal religions hide in the shadows and try avoid drawing attention, the Left Handed openly rebel against the kingdom and the Pantheistic Church, targeting those institutes through acts of terror, vandalism and orgies in plain sight. While the Church works tirelessly to root out the heresy, they have never managed to completely eradicate the Left Handed- their members either self destroy themselves instead of allowing themselves to fall into questioning or somehow manage to evade the Church\u2019s forces, leaving only destruction behind. As such, there are numerous conspiracy theories surrounding the Left Handed, such as claims that nobles of high ranking protect them, or that members of the Church are, in truth, heretics who seek to bring it down from the inside. Those rumours are quickly denied by the Church, but its inability to stop the heresy makes many ponder if it truly tries to do so in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>Theurges</b>: the Black Library is the most secured institute of Awakened knowledge in the kingdom. While numerous libraries operate within its bond, the Black Library is defined by holding access to the most forbidden texts- blatant heresies, cults dedicated to infernal beings, stone pillars bearing the carvings of the pagans and hallucinated dreams influenced by the Beyond. Regardless of origin, only the theurgists who maintain the dread archive are allowed to access this information. While the Church would have loved to destroy those heretical texts, they know that in order to battle heresies they need to be able to understand them, and as such they maintain strict regulation on those who are accepted as Black Librarians, making sure that only those who can resist the temptation of heresy would be able to examine the dark secrets, and those who fall too deep generally end up vanishing from sight, either by the hands of the Church or by escaping its wrath.<br /> <br /> <b>Penitents</b>: the Petty Monastery of the Original Sin is almost considered to be heretical by many branches of the Church- dedicated for self mutilation and ecstasy, the penitent monks believe that the Eleven Great Gods are not powers of hope but of despair, and that only pain and suffering would allow them to open the Gate and achieve their blessing. While most cults holding such a terrible faith are generally executed by the Church, the Petty Monastery have managed to gain a place for itself through constant charity work and their belief that people shouldn\u2019t be brought to the order unless they come of their own violation and free will. Their faith in sins and the need to repay for them is generally expressed through life in poverty and willingness to suffer from abuse, making them a non-threat in the eyes of the kingdom\u2019s powers. However, unknown to the Church, the Monastery has many more believers than they think- many among the poorest of commoners and serfs end up accepting the dark faith, slowly making the idea of one day getting rid of the order harder and harder with each passing day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T08:51:30-07:00","id":1536801,"title":"","content":"So I thought a bit about the relation between Calls and arcana, and after a lot of considerations I came to the conclusion that I'm not that happy with having 3 Favored and 3 Banned Arcana, both because it feels like sometimes I need to struggle with the third Arcana and because I want them to be more available to those people who want Calls to coexist with Paths. As such, I decided on making a small revision- now, each Call has two associated Arcana. If you plan on substituting Paths with Calls- great! They are your Arcana for the Path. If you want them as a different splat, however, in order to have a Call you need to either have one of the associated Arcana as your favored Arcana or having 3+ dots in both of those Arcana. This would allow a later adoption of the Call by other Paths, but would still keep them as common among 1 - 2 primary Paths. In such a system, however, getting the Call would not provide you with an extra Arcana, merely with the advantages of the Call. However, you can turn one of the Arcana into Favored if you choose to take one of the Calls Banned Arcana as Inferior, and you can only do so if you have 1 or less dots in that Arcana.<br /> <br /> So under the new system, the Favored and Banned Magic for the Calls would be as follows:<br /> <br /> Cleric: Favored- Mind, Prime. Banned- Matter, Space<br /> Oracle: Favored: Fate, Prime. Banned- Forces, Matter<br /> Invoker: Favored- Forces, Prime. Banned- Death, Matter<br /> Templar: Favored: Prime, Space. Banned- Fate, Time<br /> <br /> Envoy: Favored- Fate, Mind. Banned- Prime, Spirit<br /> Heretic: Favored- Mind, Space. Banned- Death, Fate<br /> Theurge: Favored- Fate, Space. Banned- Forces, Spirit<br /> Penitent: Favored- Death, Mind. Banned- Fate, Prime<br /> <br /> Broker: Favored- Fate, Matter. Banned- Forces, Time<br /> <br /> Again, this is just a mini update. Still working on the project, will update accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}